 {"id":"REG-GONE-002","status":"pending","priority":"P2","complexity":2,"title":"Declared-table registry is served from an in-process cache with no invalidation path \u2014 declaration edits (new tables/columns) are invisible to the HTTP API until duckbrain-http.service is cycled","reasoning":"Found by the auger foreman (tick auger-2026-09-21-07-30-25, board AUG-009): auger rewrote the 'auger' namespace's declarations to a 13-table set (added bundle, bundle_member, decision.scope), but GET /api/ns/auger/tables kept serving the previously cached table listing; the auger worker cycled duckbrain-http.service with the unit's own lifecycle command and the API answered 200 ~2s later with 13/13 tables. The registry caches a namespace's declarations in-process on first read and NOTHING invalidates it when a declare rewrites them \u2014 the stale listing predates AUG-009 (edge/facet columns from an earlier tick were already missing). Symptom downstream: a declare-extended column is refused at insert with 400 'Unknown column(s)' until a restart. Same registry family as REG-GONE-001 (registry state outliving or lagging real state).","source":"auger foreman (cross-project file, commit a4fb754)","acceptance_criteria":"A declaration rewrite that adds a table or a column is reflected by GET /api/ns/<ns>/tables without a service restart; if the in-process cache is kept, the declare path explicitly invalidates it (or the declare response states the restart requirement so callers are not surprised by 400 'Unknown column(s)').","created_at":"2026-09-21 08:17:32.000000","updated_at":"2026-09-21 08:17:32.000000"}
